    rdfs:label "Evidence for Mineral Pigment Iron Oxides Ochres &c used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 848"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "RED OCHRE: BROWN RED, or SPANISH RED, (GER. Braunroth. DU. Bruinrood. DA. Bruunrødt. Sw. Brunröd. FR. Brun rouge, Rouge brun. It. Rosso bruno. Sr. Almagre colorado, Almazarron. PORT. Almagre, Almagra,) is produced by subjecting the species of earth called yellow ochre, to the action of fire, till it becomes perfectly red or nearly brown. Red ochre is much us..."@en ;
